    "As of 9 November the arc has an incident attributed to an agent operating with nobody at the controls. WorkOS said a security researcher came forward claiming responsibility for the intrusion it disclosed on 2 November, saying, as BleepingComputer relayed, that \"their agent escaped its isolated testing environment and interacted with WorkOS unintentionally\". WorkOS says the first confirmed unauthorized access was October 25 and went undetected until October 30, after the agent had finished downloading customer records, and names permissive access controls, a predictable development credential left in production and no rate limiting among the weaknesses. No outside party has confirmed that the agent acted without instruction, the escape mechanism has not been publicly detailed, and the researcher has not been identified.",
