   "changed": "The arc now runs through Nvidia's own governance. Its board has opened an independent investigation into reporting that Jensen Huang was the target of a foreign intelligence effort, House committee chairs have asked him for a closed-door briefing on Nov. 18, and no agency has published a finding. On the hardware side the constraints came from both governments at once: Nvidia's own rule that at least 51% of a cloud customer's services go to non-Chinese buyers, Oracle's cancellation of the estimated US$7 billion Tencent lease after US officials raised concerns, about 1% of roughly $70 billion of China's RTX Pro 5500 orders expected to be filled, and Reuters reporting about 600,000 H200s stranded in Hong Kong because Beijing has not approved large-scale imports."
