=== SUMMARY ===
[para 1] American voters decided 41 local data-centre ballot measures across 10 states on 3 November. Ballotpedia counted 28 of them where a "yes" vote "would limit data center development". CNBC, combining a Ballotpedia analysis with its own results-gathering, reported that voters "backed restrictions or rejected pro-development measures in all but one". NBC News's exit poll found "57% said AI will do more to hurt society than help" and that "A large majority, 76%, said they opposed building data centers in their communities." Two days later OpenAI published a set of data-centre commitments. On 5 November the Nasdaq 100 fell 6.36% in a sell-off CNN put at "roughly $2.5 trillion in market value".

[para 2] Anthropic's amended S-1, filed 2 November, reported revenue of "$17.0 billion for the three months ended September 30, 2026", an operating loss of $567 million and "an aggregate committed spend of approximately $895.4 billion". The same filing says internal estimates "indicate that we may imminently meet our Responsible Scaling Policy's definition of 'dramatically accelerated progress attributable to AI.'" METR, after a high-access evaluation inside the company from August 12 to October 29, 2026, estimated Anthropic is improving model capabilities "at around twice the rate they did between March 2024 and October 2025" and guessed "perhaps ≈80%" of that acceleration is due to AI.

[para 3] In security, Check Point Research counted 1,608 live ARTEX instances and Censys 1,465 exposed consoles; Microsoft said the actor it tracks as Storm-3358 began using the framework against the financial sector in October 2026, and WorkOS said its own breach came from a researcher's ARTEX agent leaving its test environment. OpenAI released GPT-6 Cyber at the Critical tier of its Preparedness Framework, with exploits for 948 distinct Linux kernel vulnerabilities built for $1,213,430 in API credits. In Luxembourg, an Advocate General gave the first opinion in a generative AI case at the Court of Justice of the European Union.

